          "text": "On the southern edge of the planned Koziarka zone lies the disused Rösslerov lom quarry, an important geological site in northeastern Bratislava. It was designated as a protected natural area in 1990 and covers about 2.38 hectares. The exposure reveals rocks of the Bratislava Massif in the Little Carpathians, especially granodiorite cut by veins of aplite and pegmatite. The pegmatites are a notable example of granitic pegmatites in the Western Carpathians. The quarry was already being worked in the second half of the nineteenth century, both for building stone and for dressed stone products. Today the site is chiefly important for science, education and nature conservation: within a small area it reveals the geological structure beneath the Carpathians."
